{
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "autoloader-generic",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "The app ships no composer/autoload.php, so the server registers its generic loader for lib/ and looks every class up in the file system.",
        "  A composer/composer.json with config.vendor-dir \".\", config.optimize-autoloader true, a config.autoloader-suffix and autoload.psr-4 {\"OCA\\\\Thinkfree\\\\\": \"../lib/\"} makes composer dump-autoload write composer/autoload.php with a class map; the code of the app does not change."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vendor-shadows-server",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "firebase/php-jwt v6.11.1, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 35"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "vendor/ ships 1 package that the server ships itself in a major of Nextcloud 31 to 35. Both copies define the same classes, and the autoloader that is asked first decides which version runs.",
        "  firebase/php-jwt v6.11.1, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 35"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "boot-listener",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "lib/AppInfo/Application.php:47 get()",
        "lib/AppInfo/Application.php:49 addListener()"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "boot() registers a listener or takes a service from the container in 2 places. boot() runs once for every process of the server, so each of them is built on every request. registerEventListener() in register() builds a listener only when its event fires.",
        "  lib/AppInfo/Application.php:47 get()",
        "  lib/AppInfo/Application.php:49 addListener()"
      ]
    },
